## Sample HTML

If you'd like to use this sample HTML template, copy and paste this code into a new HTML template in your PDF.co account, save it, and enter the template ID in **Create Personalized PDF**.

This layout uses A4 portrait with **0 converter margins** and its own page padding. The empty `.logo-space` area is intentional: **Insert Company Logo into PDF** places your own logo there. Keep the configured stamp at page **0**, X **36**, Y **32**, width **160**, height **40** PDF points. For a different layout, use [PDF Inspector](https://app.pdf.co/pdf-inspector).

Blank `hero_image` values omit the image section. Long copy or a large image can change pagination; inspect the rendered PDF after changing the layout or content.

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<title>{{campaign_title}} - {{customer_name}}</title>
<style>
  @page { size: A4; margin: 0; }
  * { box-sizing: border-box; }
  body { margin: 0; padding: 48px 48px 40px; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; color: #16283F; font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.55; }
  .logo-space { height: 90px; }
  .eyebrow { font-size: 10px; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: 1.8px; text-transform: uppercase; color: #60728A; }
  h1 { margin: 14px 0 12px; max-width: 560px; font-size: 42px; letter-spacing: -1.5px; line-height: 1.1; }
  .subtitle { margin: 0 0 25px; font-size: 17px; color: #60728A; }
  .rule { width: 72px; height: 5px; margin-bottom: 26px; background: {{brand_color}}; }
  .hero { display: block; width: 100%; max-height: 220px; object-fit: cover; margin: 18px 0; }
  .personal { padding: 18px 20px; background: #F0F5FC; border-left: 4px solid {{brand_color}}; margin: 0 0 26px; }
  .personal .label { color: #60728A; font-size: 10px; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: 1px; text-transform: uppercase; }
  .personal .name { font-size: 24px; font-weight: 700; margin-top: 2px; }
  h2 { font-size: 23px; line-height: 1.25; letter-spacing: -0.4px; margin: 0 0 18px; color: {{brand_color}}; }
  .greeting { margin: 0 0 10px; font-weight: 700; }
  .body-copy { margin: 0; white-space: pre-line; }
  .cta { display: inline-block; padding: 12px 19px; margin: 25px 0 30px; color: #FFF; background: {{brand_color}}; border-radius: 5px; font-size: 13px; font-weight: 700; text-decoration: none; }
  .footer { border-top: 1px solid #DAE3EF; padding-top: 16px; margin-top: 4px; color: #60728A; font-size: 10px; }
  .footer p { margin: 0 0 7px; }
  .keep { break-inside: avoid; }
  p { orphans: 3; widows: 3; }
  a { overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
</style>
</head>
<body>
  <!-- Reserved for the second PDF.co operation: Insert Company Logo into PDF. -->
  <div class="logo-space"></div>
  <div class="eyebrow">{{company_name}} / customer update</div>
  <h1>{{campaign_title}}</h1>
  <p class="subtitle">{{campaign_subtitle}}</p>
  <div class="rule"></div>
  {{#if hero_image}}<img class="hero" src="{{hero_image}}" alt="Campaign image">{{/if}}
  <div class="personal"><div class="label">Prepared for</div><div class="name">{{customer_name}}</div></div>
  <h2>{{headline}}</h2>
  <p class="greeting">Hello {{customer_name}},</p>
  <p class="body-copy">{{body_text}}</p>
  <div class="keep"><a class="cta" href="{{cta_link}}">{{cta_text}} &rarr;</a>
  <footer class="footer"><p>{{footer_text}}</p><p>&copy; {{year}} {{company_name}}</p></footer></div>
</body>
</html>
```
